{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-13953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,6\\,|=6\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-13953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f48e535706214e002125807a3f3cce07ee9c034f6ca3ddf00a515c1c69ed35bc"} {"question" "q-13953" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-13953" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "