5c1c69ed35bc"} {"question" "q-69945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-69945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-69945" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/assets/6881c7b52de83103dcfc483ec25455781a4d399653e2369d28f6924327f8ee56.png)\n\nDetermine the area $A$ of the parallelogram in the figure.\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨-3,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨1,3⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9-2 \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-11|=11\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f48e535706214e002125807a3f3cce07ee9c034f6ca3ddf00a515c1c69ed35bc"} {"question" "q-320392" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320392" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8-15 \\\\  & =-23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,-23\\,|=23\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f48e535706214e002125807a3f3cce07ee9c034f6ca3ddf00a515c1c69ed35bc"} {"question" "q-320401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320401" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "23"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨-\\frac{4}{3},7⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,-9⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (-9)-a\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =12-7a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-7a & =0 \\\\ 7a & =12 \\\\ a & =\\frac{12}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f48e535706214e002125807a3f3cce07ee9c034f6ca3ddf00a515c1c69ed35bc"} {"question" "q-320553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"} {"question" "q-320553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/state.json" "file_sha256" "ba5d740ae6edfc0dd4ab1d77e97462c1135389e5e01f019e0be785c19b5f75f5"}] "usage" {} "basis" 840 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" [